      en: "Islamic Cairo is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Egypt. The historic core area of Cairo containing a wealth of Islamic architecture covering hundreds of years. UNESCO World Heritage Site. Famous Khan el-Khalili bazaar. Numerous historic mosques. This site holds particular significance in the history of Egypt, from pharaonic heritage to modern times. Like many notable places in Egypt, it links the pharaonic heritage with present-day life along the Nile. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Egypt between the Sahara, the Nile, the Suez Canal and the Red Sea.",
