      en: "Temple of Seti I is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Egypt. A magnificent Ancient Egyptian temple complex at Abydos, known for its fine reliefs. Built by Seti I and Ramesses II. Seven shrines for different gods. Contains the 'helicopter' hieroglyphs. This site holds particular significance in the history of Egypt, from pharaonic heritage to modern times. Like many notable places in Egypt, it links the pharaonic heritage with present-day life along the Nile. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Egypt between the Sahara, the Nile, the Suez Canal and the Red Sea.",
